## Noncommercial Purposes

Every noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose, free of license
fees and royalties and without a separate agreement. This permission
applies to everyone, including individuals, companies, charities,
schools, universities, public bodies, and other organizations.

A noncommercial purpose is one that is not primarily intended for or
directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation.
The actual purpose of the use determines whether it is noncommercial,
not the user's legal status, employer, or source of funding.

Noncommercial use, research, education, experimentation, personal
financial planning, modification, hosting, and sharing are all permitted.
These are examples, not an exhaustive list. Personal purchases and
savings do not by themselves make private financial planning commercial.
Receiving donations, grants, or a salary does not by itself make a use
commercial. All other conditions of these terms, including preservation
of notices when sharing copies, still apply.

Commercial purposes include business operations, paid services,
monetized hosting, and sale or licensing of copies when the purpose
is primarily intended for or directed toward commercial advantage or
monetary compensation. This applies to unchanged and modified copies
and copies bundled with other products. Providing the software without
charge does not make an otherwise commercial purpose noncommercial.

## Commercial Agreements

Commercial purposes are not permitted under these terms. Before using,
modifying, or distributing the software for a commercial purpose, you
must obtain a separate written commercial license agreement signed by
you and the licensor. That agreement must identify the software and
the commercial rights it grants. Fees or royalties, if any, are agreed
individually in that agreement. The licensor is not obliged to offer
a commercial agreement. These terms do not grant a commercial
trial, set a royalty rate, or automatically transfer revenue to the licensor.

